From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: emuTOS-MCD <darekadumon@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 20:57:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 156/185] Revert the visit pause: it was trading the FAT for a
 light

v24's CDBPAUSE after each visit put the access light out, and the next
headless run read a FAT with 95 phantom free clusters and a directory
with no files: after a pause, the first sector CDCSTAT announces can be
the hover's, not the target's, and the loop takes what it is announced.
Caught by the harness before it ever reached a disc. Until the loop
verifies the header CDCTRN hands it, the drive stays playing between
reads and the light stays on. The light is cosmetic; the FAT is not.

Also: CDTEST stamps every GEMDOS op with hz_200, so "the folder takes
too long" arrives as numbers -- in the emulator Dfree (the FAT walk)
already dominates at 145-205 ms against 5-35 ms for everything else.
---
 bios/scdapi.h  |  2 +-
 bios/segacd2.S | 39 +++++++++++----------------------------
 2 files changed, 12 insertions(+), 29 deletions(-)

diff --git a/bios/scdapi.h b/bios/scdapi.h
index 52d03da..ee187bb 100644
--- a/bios/scdapi.h
+++ b/bios/scdapi.h
@@ -28,7 +28,7 @@
 #define SCDAPI_H
 
 #define SCD_COOKIE   0x53674344L        /* 'SgCD' */
-#define SCD_VERSION  24
+#define SCD_VERSION  25
 
 /* Everything the disc diagnostic prints, in one go. Taken in a single
  * call rather than twenty accessors so that the numbers in one report
diff --git a/bios/segacd2.S b/bios/segacd2.S
index 68582a8..b6f926d 100644
--- a/bios/segacd2.S
+++ b/bios/segacd2.S
@@ -738,7 +738,7 @@ brd_read:
         addi.l  #0x0800,8(a5)
         subq.l  #1,4(a5)
         bne     brd_stat
-        bra     brd_park                // delivered: settle the drive
+        bra     brd_park                // delivered
 
         // Each stage names itself: 2 the firmware never reported ready,
         // 3 no sector was ever announced, 4 one was announced and never
@@ -776,34 +776,17 @@ brd_fail_read:
         // interrupt frame thrown away. Either way a5 and the scratch
         // stack are the only things it may assume, which is why the
         // stack it has to go back to lives at 44(a5) and not in a6.
-        // A successful visit leaves the drive paused, not playing.
-        //
-        // ROMREADN commands play and nothing here ever commanded
-        // anything else, so the drive kept reading into the void after
-        // every visit: the access light on for the rest of the session,
-        // the head drifting downstream, the next visit paying a seek
-        // back. The 60-second standby never helped because it talks
-        // through our own VBL commander, and the commander is off while
-        // the timeshare is armed.
-        //
-        // CDBPAUSE, then a few of the firmware's own exchanges so the
-        // command actually reaches the drive -- a posted command with
-        // no exchange behind it is the posted-to-nobody mistake again.
-        // Sega's flow pauses between reads, and a read issued from the
-        // pause hover starts instantly. Failure paths skip this: their
-        // firmware may be mid-call and their drive state is unknown.
+        // No pause here, and the scar is worth keeping visible: v24
+        // sent CDBPAUSE at the end of every successful visit to put the
+        // access light out, and the very next headless run read a FAT
+        // with 95 phantom free clusters and a directory with no files
+        // in it. After a pause, the first sector CDCSTAT announces can
+        // be the hover's sector rather than the target, and this loop
+        // takes what it is announced. Until the loop verifies the
+        // header it is handed (12(a5), CDCTRN fills it), the drive
+        // stays playing between reads and the light stays on. The
+        // light is cosmetic; the FAT is not.
 brd_park:
-        move.w  #0x0084,d0              // CDBPAUSE
-        move.w  d0,50(a5)
-        jsr     0x5F22
-        move.l  _segacd_bios_frames,d2
-        addq.l  #6,d2                   // ~0.1 s of exchanges
-        move.l  #0x60000,d3             // ...bounded by spin regardless
-1:      subq.l  #1,d3
-        beq     brd_done
-        cmp.l   _segacd_bios_frames,d2
-        bhi     1b
-
 brd_done:
         ori.w   #0x0700,sr              // shut the door before swapping back
 
